Description: Sparse R implementation of SpringRank (De Bacco, Larremore and
    Moore 2018, <doi:10.1126/sciadv.aar8260>) for ranking nodes of directed,
    weighted networks such as worker flows between employers. Ranks are obtained
    from one sparse linear system solved by preconditioned conjugate gradients,
    so networks with millions of nodes and edges can be ranked. Also provides
    the inverse temperature (hierarchy steepness), edge-direction predictions,
    violation rates, the permutation test for hierarchy, and a Poisson
    bootstrap for standard errors. This is an unofficial port of the Python
    package 'SpringRank' by the Larremore Lab; it is not affiliated with or
    endorsed by the original authors.
